\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textsc  {Biotx100} after removing the three training duplicates: 97 candidates, 75 with an interacting pair. The deployed filter's precision is not significantly above accepting everything (one-sided exact binomial $p = 0.071$), which is the audit's point. On this block the verifier buys precision ($0.843 \to 0.903$) and pays recall for it, ending \emph  {below} the filter on F1; the difference is not significant either way (McNemar $p = 0.646$, 8 fixes against 11 breaks). $\tau $ is fitted on the other two blocks, never on this one. Verifier figures average three checkpoints' probabilities, which is an ensemble; per-seed figures are in Table~\ref  {tab:perseed}.\relax }}{3}{table.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:headline}{{1}{3}{\textsc {Biotx100} after removing the three training duplicates: 97 candidates, 75 with an interacting pair. The deployed filter's precision is not significantly above accepting everything (one-sided exact binomial $p = 0.071$), which is the audit's point. On this block the verifier buys precision ($0.843 \to 0.903$) and pays recall for it, ending \emph {below} the filter on F1; the difference is not significant either way (McNemar $p = 0.646$, 8 fixes against 11 breaks). $\tau $ is fitted on the other two blocks, never on this one. Verifier figures average three checkpoints' probabilities, which is an ensemble; per-seed figures are in Table~\ref {tab:perseed}.\relax }{table.caption.7}{}}
