\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The deployed filter's 26 triple-level false positives by mechanism, and what survives the verifier at an illustrative $\tau = 0.219$. This is a diagnostic of \emph  {what the failures are}, not an operating-point result: $\tau = 0.219$ is not the threshold reported anywhere else in this paper, and the per-row mechanism grades behind this figure are not in our release (see Limitations). The three per-class rates ($10/11$, $7/8$, $5/7$) are not distinguishable from one another at these cell sizes and we claim no differential.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
